{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M7J7W9674MT3VD"}],"opens":"A source can be relied on and read purely only if one can know whether its content changed, by a hash, a version or an ETag; keeping its past is the integration's choice, an FTP reader caching what it reads becoming a store of its own.","restsOn":[],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M7J7W9674MT436","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Content identity, not history"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M7J7W9674MT31V"},{"$ref":"1M7J7W9674MT369"}],"opens":"A reference into any source, read where a type is asked, resolves in place to a value of that type, at a point, a head or now: a search bar's buffer read as a string, a git blob as text, a channel as a signal. Whether it is first class, and whether the type, the source or both resolve, is open; the session's lean, both, a mismatch refused.","restsOn":[],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M7J7W9674MT437","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Resolution where sources meet types"}
